00:05:20.426 --> 00:05:21.423
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:05:21.423 --> 00:05:23.025
I love that you're on an airplane going,

00:05:23.025 --> 00:05:24.050
it's gotta be perfect.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:25.940
(laughing)

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:26.835
Well, tell us about,

00:05:26.835 --> 00:05:28.468
I actually found out about
an organization that you,

00:05:28.468 --> 00:05:30.156
it's called Would Works.

00:05:30.156 --> 00:05:31.130
- Would Works, yeah.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:32.611
- W-O-U-L-D

00:05:32.611 --> 00:05:33.710
- That's right.
- Yes.

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:35.836
- My wood shop in Los Angeles partners

00:05:35.836 --> 00:05:38.601
with this company called Would Works,

00:05:38.601 --> 00:05:39.667
it's a non profit,

00:05:39.667 --> 00:05:43.205
that helps people on skid
row or homeless people,

00:05:43.205 --> 00:05:44.655
just get a leg back up.

00:05:44.655 --> 00:05:47.653
Because often people are
just dealt a bad hand

00:05:47.653 --> 00:05:48.893
of cards in life.

00:05:48.893 --> 00:05:52.325
Often it has to do with our
crazy health care system.

00:05:52.325 --> 00:05:53.557
- Or they're born into it.

00:05:53.557 --> 00:05:54.501
- Yeah, or they're born into it

00:05:54.501 --> 00:05:56.244
where all they wanna do,

00:05:56.244 --> 00:05:58.845
people just want to be
a responsible citizen.

00:05:58.845 --> 00:06:01.040
But sometimes it's hard
to get that first leg up

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:02.506
if you don't have an address,

00:06:02.506 --> 00:06:04.480
or you don't have a
social security number,

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:07.649
and so you can sign up at Would Works

00:06:07.649 --> 00:06:08.547
to perform labor.

00:06:08.547 --> 00:06:10.779
Where you're making
cutting boards or coasters,

00:06:10.779 --> 00:06:12.403
or other wood working items.

00:06:12.403 --> 00:06:14.125
And Would Works instead of,

00:06:14.125 --> 00:06:15.750
paying you in cash,

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:18.110
they pay you with something
you need to get going.

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:19.095
Like a suit of clothes,

00:06:19.095 --> 00:06:20.485
or a pair of glasses.

00:06:20.485 --> 00:06:21.318
- That's so cool.

00:06:21.318 --> 00:06:22.484
- And then the best thing is

00:06:22.484 --> 00:06:26.068
that a perspective job
employer can call Would Works

00:06:26.068 --> 00:06:27.181
and we can say,

00:06:27.181 --> 00:06:29.196
"Oh yeah Julie showed up for two weeks,

00:06:29.196 --> 00:06:33.502
she was sober, like give
her a job she's a good lady.

00:06:33.502 --> 00:06:35.935
And so it helps people get going

00:06:35.935 --> 00:06:37.433
and get on their way back to

00:06:37.433 --> 00:06:39.392
finding an address of their own.

00:06:39.392 --> 00:06:40.225
- That's a huge thing,

00:06:40.225 --> 00:06:41.808
to have somebody to call
like for your resume.

00:06:41.808 --> 00:06:42.774
That's a huge thing.

00:06:42.774 --> 00:06:43.630
- [Nick] It is, it's a good deal.

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:44.463
- Wow.

00:06:44.463 --> 00:06:45.296
(audience clapping)

00:06:45.296 --> 00:06:48.897
Well I'm a huge Parks and Recreation fan

00:06:48.897 --> 00:06:50.661
and I have a very embarrassing confession,

00:06:50.661 --> 00:06:52.907
I told him backstage.

00:06:52.907 --> 00:06:55.513
But in 2011 I tweeted,

00:06:55.513 --> 00:06:57.058
I didn't just tweet I begged

00:06:57.058 --> 00:06:59.455
to be on Parks and Recreation.

00:06:59.455 --> 00:07:02.894
Just so I could be in a
scene with Ron Swanson.

00:07:02.894 --> 00:07:04.345
Because I was obsessed.

00:07:04.345 --> 00:07:05.178
Here's the thing,

00:07:05.178 --> 00:07:06.434
I even own that I was a horrible actor,

00:07:06.434 --> 00:07:07.427
I'm a horrible actor.

00:07:07.427 --> 00:07:09.688
But I have a lot of spirit

00:07:09.688 --> 00:07:12.774
and I could have played a bad actor.

00:07:12.774 --> 00:07:13.607
I didn't get a call,

00:07:13.607 --> 00:07:17.687
it's fine, it's fine,
Amy it's fine, y'all.

00:07:17.687 --> 00:07:21.113
If we could turn back time with Cher,

00:07:21.113 --> 00:07:23.030
and you gave me a role,

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:25.759
what do you think I could have played,

00:07:25.759 --> 00:07:29.610
like maybe a stage five
clinger for Ron Swanson.

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:32.045
- It's a huge compliment, first of all.

00:07:32.045 --> 00:07:34.597
I'm very grateful that you
wanted to be on the show.

00:07:34.597 --> 00:07:35.470
- [Kelly] Dude, it's great.

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:36.381
It was so great,

00:07:36.381 --> 00:07:38.087
there's so many great actors on there.

00:07:38.087 --> 00:07:41.528
- Well I was grateful to
get to go to work everyday.

00:07:41.528 --> 00:07:42.525
And I think they,

00:07:42.525 --> 00:07:44.357
you know great comedy writers,

00:07:44.357 --> 00:07:46.048
they look at me and they say,

00:07:46.048 --> 00:07:48.089
"We can make people laugh

00:07:48.089 --> 00:07:50.256
with these raw materials."

00:07:51.245 --> 00:07:53.831
Give that guy a coffee cup,

00:07:53.831 --> 00:07:54.901
oh yeah here we go.

00:07:54.901 --> 00:07:57.961
Give him a phone on his belt, all right.

00:07:57.961 --> 00:07:58.794
- You know what though?

00:07:58.794 --> 00:08:00.162
The physical comedy is so key,

00:08:00.162 --> 00:08:01.534
that's what's so great.

00:08:01.534 --> 00:08:03.020
- I think they would look at you,

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:04.434
so they take your strengths.

00:08:04.434 --> 00:08:05.267
And they would say,

00:08:05.267 --> 00:08:09.100
"Okay let's cast Kelly
as a very enthusiastic,

00:08:10.121 --> 00:08:14.604
wildy enthusiastic like
hurricane of positivity.

00:08:14.604 --> 00:08:15.437
- Yes.

00:08:15.437 --> 00:08:16.675
- And I think the laugh to get

00:08:16.675 --> 00:08:17.823
with a Kelly Clarkson character

00:08:17.823 --> 00:08:20.454
is someone who would out Leslie Knop,

00:08:20.454 --> 00:08:21.581
Leslie Knope.

00:08:21.581 --> 00:08:22.414
- Exactly.

00:08:22.414 --> 00:08:24.159
- Like you would finally--

00:08:24.159 --> 00:08:25.699
- Where were you in 2011?

00:08:25.699 --> 00:08:26.937
- Someone would go too far.

00:08:26.937 --> 00:08:28.769
- (Kelly laughing) I'm just kidding.

00:08:28.769 --> 00:08:29.882
- Someone who Leslie Knope would be like,

00:08:29.882 --> 00:08:30.715
"She's too much."

00:08:30.715 --> 00:08:32.017
(audience laughing)

00:08:32.017 --> 00:08:32.852
- [Kelly] She is a little over the top.

00:08:32.852 --> 00:08:33.685
- She's too excited.

00:08:33.685 --> 00:08:35.475
- You know what, not the
first time I've heard that.

00:08:35.475 --> 00:08:36.308
(laughing)

00:08:36.308 --> 00:08:37.502
Probably not that last.

00:08:37.502 --> 00:08:39.194
My husband says it every night,

00:08:39.194 --> 00:08:40.367
and then he says, "I love you."

